  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>An easy 3.5 km walk leads to a turquoise river and an impressive 42-metre waterfall, with a view of the surrounding cliffs. One of the most spectacular spots in the Var to admire with your dog after the walk.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>An important correction to what we previously said: swimming is strictly banned at the foot of the waterfall, by municipal order, with safety fencing installed because of a risk of falling rocks — confirmed by the official website of the village of Sillans-la-Cascade. So this isn't a place to cool off with your dog, only a site to admire from the viewpoint (about 15 minutes' walk). Parking is paid from 1 April to 30 September (9am-7pm, 7 days a week), free the rest of the year. The site can also be visited with a guided tour from the local saffron grower, Yannick Dolmetta, for those who want to extend the outing. A stop at the Chapelle Saint-Laurent is also possible before or after the walk.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: come early or late in the day in summer, the site is very popular when it's hot.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Lac de Sainte-Croix is only about thirty minutes away, to extend the freshwater outing over the day.</p>
